# CODEOWNERS — module repo
#
# Maps file paths to the people/teams who must review changes to them. When a PR
# touches a matching path, GitHub auto-requests review from the owners listed.
#
# This file only REQUESTS reviewers by itself. To make owner approval MANDATORY
# before merge, the branch ruleset must set require_code_owner_review = true
# (managed in repo-governance). File + rule together = "the right people signed
# off on the code."
#
# Syntax: <path-pattern>   <owner> [<owner> ...]
#   - owners are @user or @org/team (teams need write access to the repo)
#   - LAST matching line wins, so put specific paths BELOW the catch-all
#   - replace every REPLACE-ME before relying on this
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default owner for everything in the repo (the catch-all).
*                       @DevAndOps

# CI, policy, and ownership itself — guard these tightly. Changes to who-owns-what
# or to the guardrails should go through the platform team.
/.github/               @DevAndOps
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @DevAndOps
